---
import MainLayout from '../layouts/MainLayout.astro';
import styles from './cv.module.css';
import '../styles/cv-print.css';
---

<MainLayout title="CV · Karen Dettmar">

  <div class={styles['cv-wrapper']}>

    <!-- Download button -->
    <div class={styles['cv-actions']}>
      <a href="/Karen_Dettmar_CV.pdf" download class={styles['cv-dl-btn']}>↓ &nbsp;Download PDF</a>
    </div>

    <!-- Name & identity -->
    <header class={styles['cv-header']}>
      <h1 class={styles['cv-name']}>Karen Dettmar</h1>
      <p class={styles['cv-subtitle']}>Design Engineer &nbsp;·&nbsp; New York City</p>
      <p class={styles['cv-contact']}>
        <a href="mailto:karen.dettmar@gmail.com">karen.dettmar@gmail.com</a>
        <span class={styles['cv-sep']}>·</span>
        <a href="https://linkedin.com/in/kdettmar" target="_blank">linkedin.com/in/kdettmar</a>
        <!-- On the site you are already here; on paper the address has to be
             on the page for anyone to type it. -->
        <span class="cv-print-only"><span class={styles['cv-sep']}>·</span> karendettmar.com</span>
      </p>
    </header>

    <!-- Generated Nov 3, 2026 from Career Goals/cv-tool (base.json + cuts/uxe-general.json), the same source as the downloadable PDF. Edit there and regenerate rather than by hand. -->
    <section class={styles['cv-section']}>
      <h2 class={styles['cv-section-heading']}>Skills &amp; Tools</h2>
      <div class={styles['cv-skills']}>
        <div class={styles['cv-skill-row']}>
          <span class={styles['cv-skill-cat']}>Engineering</span>
          <span class={styles['cv-skill-val']}>JavaScript, React, HTML, CSS, Node.js, REST APIs, SDK integration, responsive UI, WCAG accessibility, Git, TypeScript, Vue, Astro, Tailwind CSS</span>
        </div>
        <div class={styles['cv-skill-row']}>
          <span class={styles['cv-skill-cat']}>Design</span>
          <span class={styles['cv-skill-val']}>Figma, prototyping in code, wireframing, user flows, usability testing</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class={styles['cv-section']}>
      <h2 class={styles['cv-section-heading']}>Experience</h2>
      <div class={styles['cv-role']}>
        <div class={styles['cv-role-meta']}>
          <span class={styles['cv-role-title']}>Developer Advocate</span>
          <span class={styles['cv-role-company']}>Intuit</span>
          <span class={styles['cv-role-loc']}>New York, NY</span>
          <span class={styles['cv-role-date']}>Nov 2022 – Sept 2024</span>
        </div>
        <div class={styles['cv-role-scope']}>Design and front-end engineering for internal developer platforms</div>
        <ul class={styles['cv-bullets']}>
          <li>Designed and built a <strong class={styles['cv-em']}>React</strong> scorecard, leaderboard, and reporting interface for the scaled InnerSource Tournament, replacing the pilot's spreadsheet scoring, with a platform engineer setting up a weekly pull of each service's maturity data from the developer portal. <strong class={styles['cv-em']}>Result: 150 participants, and 40% of the services scored became ready for other teams to adopt on their own.</strong></li>
          <li>Built and shipped engineer-facing tools and interactive learning experiences used by <strong class={styles['cv-em']}>7,000+ global employees</strong>, owning the full development lifecycle from prototype through public deployment.</li>
          <li>Delivered internal training on React Security, InnerSource, OpenSource, <strong class={styles['cv-em']}>Design Systems,</strong> and documentation standards, including the design systems session in new-employee onboarding.</li>
          <li>Wrote a conference talk on <strong class={styles['cv-em']}>accessibility, WCAG and ADA compliance</strong>, accepted at <strong class={styles['cv-em']}>All Things Open</strong>.</li>
          <li>Partnered with a staff engineer and product manager to roll out <strong class={styles['cv-em']}>GitHub Copilot</strong> access to Intuit's engineering organization at a company-wide virtual AI event, building the announcement deck and a live demo of installing and using it; interviewed the AI and Data teams on the tools they had built and hosted fireside chats on the future of AI in software development.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class={styles['cv-role']}>
        <div class={styles['cv-role-meta']}>
          <span class={styles['cv-role-title']}>Developer Advocate</span>
          <span class={styles['cv-role-company']}>Wix</span>
          <span class={styles['cv-role-loc']}>New York, NY</span>
          <span class={styles['cv-role-date']}>Feb 2020 – Oct 2022</span>
        </div>
        <div class={styles['cv-role-scope']}>Product design, user research and front-end for the developer platform</div>
        <ul class={styles['cv-bullets']}>
          <li>Built the demo product for the first ever <strong class={styles['cv-em']}>Wix DevCon</strong> from scratch, on several platform services that had not yet shipped, carrying it through prototyping, QA, and approvals with PMs, engineers, marketing, and the CEO against a fixed launch date it had to work on live. <strong class={styles['cv-em']}>Result:</strong> the build surfaced and fixed platform bugs, and I presented it in the keynote to a 300-person live audience.</li>
          <li>Taught workshops on JavaScript fundamentals, UI/UX best practice, and design-to-code transitions, including a workshop that took college design students through their portfolio finals.</li>
          <li>Designed and ran a user study assessing developer experience on the platform. <strong class={styles['cv-em']}>Findings drove product, R&amp;D, and UX to ship onboarding UI updates, refreshed documentation, and new product features.</strong></li>
          <li>Asked for a new-hire onboarding deck, built an <strong class={styles['cv-em']}>onboarding site</strong> on the Wix platform instead and revised it from new-hire feedback. <strong class={styles['cv-em']}>Result: time on the homepage doubled.</strong></li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class={styles['cv-role']}>
        <div class={styles['cv-role-meta']}>
          <span class={styles['cv-role-title']}>Front End Developer</span>
          <span class={styles['cv-role-company']}>Wet Design</span>
          <span class={styles['cv-role-loc']}>Burbank, CA</span>
          <span class={styles['cv-role-date']}>Feb 2019 – Jul 2019</span>
        </div>
        <ul class={styles['cv-bullets']}>
          <li>Designed and built the front end of an internal <strong class={styles['cv-em']}>travel request and approval app</strong> that replaced a legacy system: interviewed the travel manager and frequent travelers, designed the workflow, wireframes and UI, and coded a <strong class={styles['cv-em']}>responsive single-page app</strong> in VueJS, JavaScript, HTML, SASS, and GraphQL as the sole front-end developer. <strong class={styles['cv-em']}>Result: after IT testing and a departmental pilot, it rolled out company-wide.</strong></li>
          <li>Redesigned and deployed the company intranet, consulting with the branding team on interface and technical requirements to make it the primary channel for company communication. Built and <strong class={styles['cv-em']}>usability tested</strong> its components in Confluence, CSS, and JavaScript. <strong class={styles['cv-em']}>Result: 25% increase in time on page.</strong></li>
          <li>Maintained, updated, and built <strong class={styles['cv-em']}>mobile modular components</strong> for the existing site.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class={styles['cv-role']}>
        <div class={styles['cv-role-meta']}>
          <span class={styles['cv-role-title']}>Head Designer, Print and Web</span>
          <span class={styles['cv-role-company']}>Pixomondo (PXO)</span>
          <span class={styles['cv-role-loc']}>Los Angeles, CA</span>
          <span class={styles['cv-role-date']}>Jan 2018 – Jan 2019</span>
        </div>
        <ul class={styles['cv-bullets']}>
          <li>Redesigned and implemented the company website, meeting regularly with the CEO on design direction. Built on a <strong class={styles['cv-em']}>LEMP stack (CentOS, NGINX, MySQL, PHP)</strong> with a <strong class={styles['cv-em']}>WordPress theme written from scratch. Result: 10% increase in page visits</strong>, and the redesign was what made the campaign launch on schedule.</li>
          <li>Built a <strong class={styles['cv-em']}>Raspberry Pi conference room booking system</strong> for the studio.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class={styles['cv-role']}>
        <div class={styles['cv-role-meta']}>
          <span class={styles['cv-role-title']}>Jr Front End Developer and Designer</span>
          <span class={styles['cv-role-company']}>CIBT</span>
          <span class={styles['cv-role-loc']}>Washington, D.C.</span>
          <span class={styles['cv-role-date']}>Jan 2017 – Nov 2017</span>
        </div>
        <ul class={styles['cv-bullets']}>
          <li>Built <strong class={styles['cv-em']}>clean, scalable, responsive templates</strong> by hand in HTML, CSS, and JavaScript, built to <strong class={styles['cv-em']}>WCAG</strong> standards.</li>
          <li>Ran on-site polls on the visa requirements page and the application funnel to find out why travelers were leaving. When the first round returned thin answers, redesigned the survey to open with a yes/no question before the open one. <strong class={styles['cv-em']}>Result: one week of the redesigned survey drew more than double what five weeks of the original had</strong>, and the coded responses ranked the blockers, led by unclear requirements.</li>
          <li>Maintained and redesigned components for multilingual company sites, providing bespoke landing pages for high-profile corporate clients (<strong class={styles['cv-em']}>Microsoft, Apple, IBM</strong>) alongside the consumer-facing traveler experience.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class={`${styles['cv-section']} ${styles['cv-section-last']}`}>
      <h2 class={styles['cv-section-heading']}>Education</h2>
      <div class={styles['cv-edu-list']}>
        <div class={styles['cv-edu-item']}>
          <span class={styles['cv-edu-degree']}>Certification in Fashion Design</span>
          <span class={styles['cv-edu-school']}>Parsons School of Design – The New School &nbsp;·&nbsp; Full-time 2025</span>
        </div>
        <div class={styles['cv-edu-item']}>
          <span class={styles['cv-edu-degree']}>Full Stack Web Development Program: MEAN, Ruby on Rails, Python &amp; Django</span>
          <span class={styles['cv-edu-school']}>Coding Dojo &nbsp;·&nbsp; Washington, D.C.</span>
        </div>
        <div class={styles['cv-edu-item']}>
          <span class={styles['cv-edu-degree']}>B.A. Studio Art (Printmaking) &nbsp;·&nbsp; B.A. Politics (Foreign Affairs)</span>
          <span class={styles['cv-edu-school']}>University of Virginia</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>

</MainLayout>
